Fixed: The boundary condition objects of the incompressible Navier-Stokes integrators hold the registered physical boundary conditions as soon as they are registered. They previously held homogeneous conditions until the first time step, so IBAMR::INSCollocatedHierarchyIntegrator removed part of the initial velocity in its initial projection. A run without velocity initial conditions still uses homogeneous conditions until its first time step.
<br>
